          %h2#dependent_function_types_as_types_of_dependent_anafunctions Dependent function types as types of dependent anafunctions
          %p
            In the same way that one could define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+types"} equivalence types
            as types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-to-one+correspondences"} one-to-one correspondences
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            as types of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctions"} anafunctions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+function+types"} dependent function types
            as types of dependent anafunctions. This requires both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+heterogeneous+identity+types"} indexed heterogeneous identity types
            being defined first, which we shall write as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a =_A b
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %msubsup
                    %mo =
                    %mi B
                    %mi p
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_{B}^{p} y
            respectively for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:a =_A b
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:B(a)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:B(b)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
